index 000000000..2b0d300f0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/fabelgeist-hair/src/lib.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,187 @@
+//! Strand hair after Rosu et al., *DiffLocks: Generating 3D Hair from a
+//! Single Image using Diffusion Models* (CVPR 2025) -- the synthetic-data
+//! half of it: how its 40K hairstyles are made, and then how to draw them,
+//! from film to phone.
+//!
+//! # Making hair
+//!
+//! DiffLocks grows every hairstyle in Blender with geometry nodes. A base
+//! style is a few dozen hand-drawn guide strands; a stack of Blender's hair
+//! node groups interpolates them to ~100K strands over the scalp, then
+//! clumps, curls and noises them -- each several times at different scales
+//! -- shrinkwraps them off the body and drapes them under random gravity and
+//! wind. 110 parameters, each drawn from a range, make every sample
+//! different. The same pipeline here:
+//!
+//! * [`Strands`]: curves of equal point count with the attributes the node
+//!   groups pass between them (root UV and normal, a stable ID, the parting
+//!   group, the guide map).
+//! * [`ops`]: the node groups themselves, written out from their node
+//!   graphs -- `Interpolate Hair Curves`, `Clump Hair Curves`, `Curl Hair
+//!   Curves`, `Frizz Hair Curves`, `Hair Curves Noise`, `Trim`, `Smooth`,
+//!   `Shrinkwrap Hair Curves` with `Restore Curve Segment Length`, `Create
+//!   Guide Index Map`, `Set Hair Curve Profile` and their `shape_range`
+//!   falloff -- plus waves ([`ops::Wave`]), each strand's root turned to its
+//!   follicle ([`ops::Orient`]) and the drape ([`ops::Settle`]), run in
+//!   parallel over strands.
+//! * [`Groom`]: a stack of operations, serialisable, the recipe of one
+//!   hairstyle; [`Look`] a stack built from the few knobs that mean
+//!   something to a person, in DiffLocks' order, and drawn at random the way
+//!   the dataset draws.
+//! * [`Hairdo`]: what shapes the guides, as three choices made apart --
+//!   the [`Follicles`] (the growth pattern, [`Growth`]: a crown whorl, two,
+//!   a cowlick, forward, back...; the angle hair leaves the scalp at, how
+//!   far it keeps its follicle's direction, how thick it is, how evenly it
+//!   covers the scalp, the [`Hairline`]'s shape), the [`Haircut`] (lengths
+//!   over the head, a hemline, clippers, a fringe, a dome: [`Cut`] names
+//!   the usual ones) and the [`Hairstyle`] (parted, swept, slicked back,
+//!   stood up, tied: [`Arrangement`]) -- grown as guides on a [`Head`] (a
+//!   mannequin bust as a distance field, which is also the scalp,
+//!   [`Surface`], and the collider, [`Collider`]). [`Preset`] names
+//!   twenty-four hairdos: every kind of hair the paper's figures show
+//!   ([`Preset::PAPER`]: bob, crop, long, shag, bowl cut, ringlets, afro,
+//!   quiff, balding and more) and some it lacks (ponytail, bun, braid,
+//!   dreadlocks, mohawk).
+//! * [`HairMaterial`]: the Chiang hair BSDF's parameters, melanin and
+//!   redness as Blender's Principled Hair takes them.
+//! * [`dataset`] and the `hair-dataset` binary: samples on disk in the
+//!   dataset's own layout (`full_strands.npz`, the density map, metadata,
+//!   a render), and [`export`]: NumPy, USC-HairSalon `.data`, PLY scalps.
+//!
+//! # Drawing hair
+//!
+//! [`HairLods`] prepares a groom once into every form it can be drawn in --
+//! the strands at several point counts in one shuffled order (so any prefix
+//! is an even sample, and fewer strands is just a smaller count), hair cards
+//! cut from the groom's own locks with a painted atlas, and occlusion baked
+//! into every point. A [`LodPolicy`] picks the form from the head's size on
+//! screen for a target -- cinematic, desktop or mobile -- with its shading.
+//! [`render::HairRenderer`] draws it: camera-facing ribbons from a storage
+//! buffer, Marschner's lobes in Karis' fit (or Kajiya-Kay on mobile), deep
+//! opacity maps from the key light, stochastic transparency so sub-pixel
+//! strands add up to their true density, and a jittered running mean that
+//! converges to a supersampled still. `hair-viewer` shows it all live.
+//!
+//! # Moving hair
+//!
+//! [`sim::HairSim`] runs real-time physics, optionally: some of the groom's
+//! strands simulated as elastic rods ([`rod`]: Cosserat rods with hair's
+//! own stiffness and mass, under gravity, in the air, clamped in follicles
+//! a moving head carries, kept off its distance field, each step implicit
+//! and solved exactly; the groom their equilibrium under gravity), every
+//! drawn strand following the ones nearest its root in a compute pass, and
+//! moving frames blended over time so the stochastic coverage does not
+//! sparkle. On the GPU
+//! ([`gpu::GpuSim`]) the strands also meet: hair denser than at rest is
+//! pushed apart (its volume kept), hair moving through hair drags it along,
+//! and strands collide, segment against segment. How many strands, of how
+//! many points, is a level of detail of its own ([`sim::SimLevel`]), chosen
+//! by the head's size on screen like the drawing's.
+//!
+//! # On the GPU
+//!
+//! All of it runs on the GPU as well ([`gpu`], the `gpu` feature): the
+//! guides, the groom, its levels of detail and cards, the head's cover and
+//! the physics are compute kernels on the compute layer, and what they
+//! make is drawn from the buffers they wrote -- a hundred thousand strands
+//! grown and prepared in tens of milliseconds, where the host takes a
+//! second or two; the scalp they root on is cut there too, when the
+//! hairline changes. The viewer, the dataset and the snapshots groom
+//! there. The host path stays, the reference the kernels are tested
+//! against (the scalp to its triangles, the guides to a micrometre) and the
+//! way without a GPU.
+//!
+//! # Where this departs from the paper
+//!
+//! * **The body.** DiffLocks grows hair on the SMPL-X scalp and collides it
+//!   with the SMPL-X body; SMPL-X is not ours to ship. The [`Head`] is a
+//!   bust of unioned ellipsoids and capsules; any scalp with a UV map loads
+//!   in its place ([`Surface::from_ply`] reads DiffLocks' `scalp.ply`).
+//! * **The base styles** are 75 hand-drawn sets of guides in the paper and
+//!   not published. Here each style is grown: every guide leaves its
+//!   follicle as the growth pattern points, rises to the layer of hair
+//!   beneath it, lies along the head as combed while it is supported, and
+//!   bends as a cantilever under its own weight once free, until the cut
+//!   ends it ([`hairdo`]). Every strand's root is then turned to its own
+//!   follicle ([`ops::Orient`]), which interpolating guides a few
+//!   centimetres apart would blur.
+//! * **Interpolation** takes a strand count rather than a density, fades
+//!   `Follow Surface Normal`'s turn out along the strand (Blender turns the
+//!   whole strand, which on a curved scalp swings long hair's tips out), and
+//!   blends only guides whose courses agree: the mean of a guide combed
+//!   left and one combed right would run down the face between them.
+//! * **The drape** is each strand's static equilibrium as an elastic rod
+//!   against the head's field ([`ops::Settle`]), not Blender's cloth solver,
+//!   and applies the *change* from standard gravity and still air -- so it
+//!   blows and lifts a style without sagging it into another. It runs on
+//!   the guides, and the full groom inherits it.
+//! * **Frizz and noise** are Blender's, with two changes: frizz takes a
+//!   share of flyaway strands (the rest barely wander) and can wander
+//!   smoothly, and the look uses noise as offsets, not Blender's cumulative
+//!   walk, whose reach grows with the point count.
+//! * **Rendering.** DiffLocks path-traces the Chiang BSDF under HDRIs.
+//!   Here rendering is rasterised and real time; the Chiang absorption is
+//!   exported with every sample for an offline renderer, and the real-time
+//!   colour is Chiang's colour mapping over a quarter of it, matched to
+//!   Cycles by eye ([`HairMaterial::base_color`]).
+//!
+//! ```no_run
+//! use fabelgeist_hair::{Arrangement, Cut, Growth, HairLods, Haircut, Head, LodSettings, Look, Preset};
+//!
+//! // A long cut worn in a ponytail, from a double crown.
+//! let mut look = Look::new(Preset::Long);
+//! look.hairdo.follicles.growth = Growth::DoubleWhorl;
+//! look.hairdo.haircut = Haircut::new(Cut::Layered);
+//! look.hairdo.hairstyle = fabelgeist_hair::Hairstyle::new(Arrangement::Ponytail);
+//!
+//! let head = look.head(&Head::mannequin());
+//! let scalp = head.scalp(0.004);
+//! let hair = look.grow(&head, &scalp);
+//! let lods = HairLods::build(&hair, head.cranium.center, Some(&head), &LodSettings::default());
+//! ```
+
+pub mod cards;
+pub mod collider;
+pub mod cover;
+pub mod dataset;
+pub mod difflocks;
+pub mod export;
+pub mod follicles;
+#[cfg(feature = "gpu")]
+pub mod gpu;
+pub mod grid;
+pub mod groom;
+pub mod haircut;
+pub mod hairdo;
+pub mod hairstyle;
+pub mod head;
+pub mod identity;
+pub mod lod;
+pub mod look;
+pub mod material;
+pub mod noise;
+pub mod occlusion;
+pub mod ops;
+pub mod parameters;
+pub mod presets;
+#[cfg(feature = "render")]
+pub mod render;
+pub mod rng;
+pub mod rod;
+pub mod sim;
+pub mod strands;
+pub mod surface;
+
+pub use collider::{Collider, MeshCollider};
+pub use follicles::{Follicles, Growth, Hairline};
+pub use groom::Groom;
+pub use haircut::{Cut, Fringe, Haircut};
+pub use hairdo::Hairdo;
+pub use hairstyle::{Arrangement, Hairstyle};
+pub use head::Head;
+pub use lod::{Blend, HairLods, LodCounts, LodPolicy, LodSettings, Representation};
+pub use look::Look;
+pub use material::{HairMaterial, Taper};
+pub use presets::Preset;
+pub use strands::Strands;
+pub use surface::Surface;
diff --git a/crates/fabelgeist-hair/src/lod.rs b/crates/fabelgeist-hair/src/lod.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..efd144513
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/fabelgeist-hair/src/lod.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,557 @@
+//! Levels of detail: one groom, drawn from film to phone.
+//!
+//! A groom is prepared once ([`HairLods::build`]) into every form it can be
+//! drawn in:
+//!
+//! * **Strand levels.** The strands at their full point count, and at a
+//!   half, a quarter and a few points each -- each coarse strand kept off
+//!   the head where its straight segments would cut through the curve of
+//!   the scalp ([`keep_clear`]), or the hair would thin to bald patches
+//!   with distance. Every level keeps the strands
+//!   in one shuffled order (by a hash of each strand's ID), so the first
+//!   `n` strands of any level are an even random sample of the whole head:
+//!   drawing fewer strands is drawing a shorter prefix -- no rebuild, no
+//!   popping, just a count. Fewer strands are drawn wider, by the inverse of
+//!   the share drawn, so the head's coverage holds (Yuksel's and every
+//!   game's strand culling).
+//! * **Cards** ([`crate::cards`]): a few thousand strips following the
+//!   locks, for distance and for mobile, in a fine and a coarse cut.
+//! * **Occlusion** ([`crate::occlusion`]) baked into every point and card
+//!   vertex, so a level with no shadow maps still has depth.
+//! * **Scalp cover** ([`ScalpCover`]): how much hair covers the skin where
+//!   it grows, which the head is shaded by -- at every level, so no level
+//!   shows bare scalp between its strands.
+//!
+//! A [`LodPolicy`] then picks a form from how tall the head is on screen,
+//! in pixels, with a shading [`Quality`] to go with it. Near the bottom of
+//! each band the next coarser form fades in ([`LodPolicy::select_blended`]):
+//! strands hand over to the coarser level strand by strand along the shared
+//! order, cards dissolve in card by card as the strands thin out -- so moving
+//! away never pops. The three policies
+//! are the three targets the hair is for: [`LodPolicy::cinematic`] (every
+//! strand, every point, deep opacity shadows, accumulated over jittered
+//! frames), [`LodPolicy::desktop`] and [`LodPolicy::mobile`].
+
+use fabelgeist_math::Vec3;
+use rayon::prelude::*;
+
+use crate::cards::{CardAtlas, CardMesh, CardSettings};
+use crate::collider::{Collider, keep_clear};
+use crate::cover::ScalpCover;
+use crate::occlusion::{Occlusion, OcclusionSettings};
+use crate::rng;
+use crate::sim::SimLevel;
+use crate::strands::{Strands, resample_into};
+
+/// How far off the head a coarse strand's segments are kept, metres: about
+/// where the groom's own strands lie over the scalp.
+const STRAND_CLEARANCE: f32 = 0.0012;
+
+/// A strand's per-strand data as the strand shader reads it.
+#[repr(C)]
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, bytemuck::Pod, bytemuck::Zeroable)]
+pub struct StrandInfo {
+    /// Root radius, metres.
+    pub radius: f32,
+    /// 0 to 1, per strand.
+    pub random: f32,
+    pub uv: [f32; 2],
+}
+
+/// Every strand at one point count, in the shared shuffled order.
+pub struct StrandLevel {
+    pub points: usize,
+    /// Position and baked sky visibility, strand-major.
+    pub positions: Vec<[f32; 4]>,
+    pub strands: Vec<StrandInfo>,
+}
+
+impl StrandLevel {
+    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {
+        self.strands.len()
+    }
+
+    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {
+        self.strands.is_empty()
+    }
+
+    pub fn bytes(&self) -> usize {
+        self.positions.len() * 16 + self.strands.len() * 16
+    }
+}
+
+pub struct LodSettings {
+    /// Points per strand at each level after the first (which keeps the
+    /// groom's own count); a level is dropped if it would not be coarser.
+    pub strand_points: Vec<usize>,
+    pub cards: Vec<CardSettings>,
+    pub occlusion: OcclusionSettings,
+    pub atlas_variants: u32,
+    pub atlas_size: [u32; 2],
+}
+
+impl Default for LodSettings {
+    fn default() -> Self {
+        Self {
+            strand_points: vec![24, 12, 6],
+            cards: vec![
+                CardSettings::default(),
+                CardSettings {
+                    size: 0.016,
+                    segments: 6,
+                    width_scale: 1.5,
+                    min_strands: 4,
+                },
+            ],
+            occlusion: OcclusionSettings::default(),
+            atlas_variants: 8,
+            atlas_size: [64, 256],
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// A groom ready to draw at any distance.
+pub struct HairLods {
+    pub levels: Vec<StrandLevel>,
+    pub cards: Vec<CardMesh>,
+    pub atlas: CardAtlas,
+    pub bounds: [Vec3; 2],
+    /// The head's centre, for card orientation and framing.
+    pub center: Vec3,
+    /// How much hair covers the skin, for shading the head under it.
+    pub cover: ScalpCover,
+}
+
+impl HairLods {
+    pub fn build(
+        strands: &Strands,
+        center: Vec3,
+        body: Option<&dyn Collider>,
+        settings: &LodSettings,
+    ) -> Self {
+        let occlusion = Occlusion::bake(strands, body, &settings.occlusion);
+        let mut order: Vec<usize> = (0..strands.len()).collect();
+        order.sort_by_key(|&s| rng::hash(strands.id[s].word(), 0x0D3E));
+
+        let mut counts = vec![strands.points];
+        for &p in &settings.strand_points {
+            if p >= 2 && p < *counts.last().unwrap() {
+                counts.push(p);
+            }
+        }
+        let info: Vec<StrandInfo> = order
+            .iter()
+            .map(|&s| StrandInfo {
+                radius: strands.radius[s],
+                random: rng::unit(strands.id[s].word(), 0x5EED),
+                uv: strands.root_uv[s],
+            })
+            .collect();
+        let levels = counts
+            .iter()
+            .map(|&points| {
+                let positions: Vec<[f32; 4]> = order
+                    .par_iter()
+                    .flat_map_iter(|&s| {
+                        let mut out = vec![Vec3::default(); points];
+                        if points == strands.points {
+                            out.copy_from_slice(strands.strand(s));
+                        } else {
+                            resample_into(strands.strand(s), &mut Vec::new(), &mut out);
+                            if let Some(body) = body {
+                                keep_clear(body, &mut out, STRAND_CLEARANCE, 4);
+                            }
+                        }
+                        out.into_iter().map(|p| {
+                            let [x, y, z] = p.to_array();
+                            [x, y, z, occlusion.at(p)]
+                        })
+                    })
+                    .collect();
+                StrandLevel {
+                    points,
+                    positions,
+                    strands: info.clone(),
+                }
+            })
+            .collect();
+        let cards = settings
+            .cards
+            .iter()
+            .map(|c| {
+                CardMesh::build(
+                    strands,
+                    center,
+                    Some(&occlusion),
+                    body,
+                    c,
+                    settings.atlas_variants,
+                )
+            })
+            .collect();
+        let [w, h] = settings.atlas_size;
+        Self {
+            levels,
+            cards,
+            atlas: CardAtlas::paint(settings.atlas_variants, w, h, 0xA71A5),
+            bounds: strands.bounds(),
+            center,
+            cover: ScalpCover::new(strands),
+        }
+    }
+
+    pub fn strand_count(&self) -> usize {
+        self.levels.first().map_or(0, |l| l.len())
+    }
+
+    /// How many strands, levels and card levels there are: all a
+    /// [`LodPolicy`] needs to choose among them.
+    pub fn counts(&self) -> LodCounts {
+        LodCounts {
+            strands: self.strand_count(),
+            levels: self.levels.len(),
+            cards: self.cards.len(),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// The sizes of a groom's levels of detail, wherever they were built: the
+/// host's [`HairLods`] or the GPU's [`crate::gpu::GpuLods`].
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct LodCounts {
+    /// The strands of the finest level.
+    pub strands: usize,
+    /// The strand levels.
+    pub levels: usize,
+    /// The card levels.
+    pub cards: usize,
+}
+
+/// How the hair is shaded.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]
+pub struct Quality {
+    /// Marschner's three lobes (Karis' fit) with multiple scattering, or
+    /// Kajiya-Kay with two shifted highlights.
+    pub marschner: bool,
+    /// Deep opacity shadows from the key light; without them only the
+    /// baked occlusion darkens.
+    pub shadows: bool,
+    /// Deep opacity map size.
+    pub shadow_resolution: u32,
+    /// Frames accumulated with sub-pixel jitter while the view holds still.
+    pub accumulate: u32,
+    /// Narrowest a strand is drawn, pixels; narrower strands fade instead.
+    pub min_pixels: f32,
+}
+
+/// A coarser form fading in under the one a band draws: `amount` of the way
+/// from the band's own form to `to`.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]
+pub struct Blend {
+    pub to: Representation,
+    pub amount: f32,
+}
+
+/// What to draw this frame.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]
+pub enum Representation {
+    /// The first `count` strands of `level`, `width_scale` times as wide.
+    Strands {
+        level: usize,
+        count: usize,
+        width_scale: f32,
+    },
+    Cards {
+        level: usize,
+    },
+}
+
+/// A band of on-screen sizes and what is drawn in it.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]
+pub struct Band {
+    /// The head is at least this many pixels tall.
+    pub min_pixels: f32,
+    pub form: Form,
+}
+
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]
+pub enum Form {
+    /// A share of the strands at a level.
+    Strands {
+        level: usize,
+        share: f32,
+    },
+    Cards {
+        level: usize,
+    },
+}
+
+#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
+pub struct LodPolicy {
+    pub name: &'static str,
+    /// From the largest on screen down.
+    pub bands: Vec<Band>,
+    pub quality: Quality,
+    /// Shadows are cast by this strand level and share, whatever is drawn.
+    pub shadow_level: usize,
+    pub shadow_share: f32,
+    /// Over how much of a band's lower edge, as a share of it, the next
+    /// coarser form fades in: 0.4 fades from 1.4 times the edge down to it.
+    pub blend: f32,
+    /// How finely the hair is simulated, by the head's height on screen in
+    /// pixels, largest first: each level from its height up.
+    pub sim: Vec<(f32, SimLevel)>,
+}
+
+impl LodPolicy {
+    /// Every strand at every point, always.
+    pub fn cinematic() -> Self {
+        Self {
+            name: "Cinematic",
+            bands: vec![Band {
+                min_pixels: 0.0,
+                form: Form::Strands {
+                    level: 0,
+                    share: 1.0,
+                },
+            }],
+            quality: Quality {
+                marschner: true,
+                shadows: true,
+                shadow_resolution: 2048,
+                accumulate: 64,
+                min_pixels: 0.5,
+            },
+            shadow_level: 0,
+            shadow_share: 1.0,
+            blend: 0.0,
+            sim: vec![(0.0, SimLevel::HIGH)],
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// Strands close up, thinning with distance, cards far away. Every
+    /// strand until the head is under 300 pixels tall -- a head in a
+    /// medium shot at 1080p -- so what is coarser only shows where too
+    /// little of it is on screen to tell.
+    pub fn desktop() -> Self {
+        Self {
+            name: "Desktop",
+            bands: vec![
+                Band {
+                    min_pixels: 300.0,
+                    form: Form::Strands {
+                        level: 0,
+                        share: 1.0,
+                    },
+                },
+                Band {
+                    min_pixels: 150.0,
+                    form: Form::Strands {
+                        level: 1,
+                        share: 0.5,
+                    },
+                },
+                Band {
+                    min_pixels: 70.0,
+                    form: Form::Strands {
+                        level: 2,
+                        share: 0.2,
+                    },
+                },
+                Band {
+                    min_pixels: 32.0,
+                    form: Form::Cards { level: 0 },
+                },
+                Band {
+                    min_pixels: 0.0,
+                    form: Form::Cards { level: 1 },
+                },
+            ],
+            quality: Quality {
+                marschner: true,
+                shadows: true,
+                shadow_resolution: 1024,
+                accumulate: 8,
+                min_pixels: 1.0,
+            },
+            shadow_level: 2,
+            shadow_share: 0.25,
+            blend: 0.4,
+            sim: vec![
+                (260.0, SimLevel::HIGH),
+                (110.0, SimLevel::MEDIUM),
+                (0.0, SimLevel::LOW),
+            ],
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// A fifth of the strands close up, a tenth further, cards far away;
+    /// cheap shading and only baked shadowing.
+    pub fn mobile() -> Self {
+        Self {
+            name: "Mobile",
+            bands: vec![
+                Band {
+                    min_pixels: 300.0,
+                    form: Form::Strands {
+                        level: 2,
+                        share: 0.2,
+                    },
+                },
+                Band {
+                    min_pixels: 140.0,
+                    form: Form::Strands {
+                        level: 3,
+                        share: 0.1,
+                    },
+                },
+                Band {
+                    min_pixels: 55.0,
+                    form: Form::Cards { level: 0 },
+                },
+                Band {
+                    min_pixels: 0.0,
+                    form: Form::Cards { level: 1 },
+                },
+            ],
+            quality: Quality {
+                marschner: false,
+                shadows: false,
+                shadow_resolution: 512,
+                accumulate: 1,
+                min_pixels: 1.0,
+            },
+            shadow_level: 3,
+            shadow_share: 0.1,
+            blend: 0.4,
+            sim: vec![(220.0, SimLevel::MEDIUM), (0.0, SimLevel::LOW)],
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// How finely to simulate a head `pixels` tall.
+    pub fn sim_level(&self, pixels: f32) -> SimLevel {
+        self.sim
+            .iter()
+            .find(|(min, _)| pixels >= *min)
+            .or(self.sim.last())
+            .map_or(SimLevel::MEDIUM, |(_, level)| *level)
+    }
+
+    /// [`LodPolicy::sim_level`], staying at `current` until the head is a
+    /// sixth past the edge it would cross: a level change rebuilds the
+    /// simulation, and a head resting on an edge should not flicker across
+    /// it.
+    pub fn sim_level_from(&self, current: SimLevel, pixels: f32) -> SimLevel {
+        let wanted = self.sim_level(pixels);
+        if wanted == current {
+            return current;
+        }
+        let rank = |level: SimLevel| self.sim.iter().position(|(_, l)| *l == level);
+        let (Some(at), Some(to)) = (rank(current), rank(wanted)) else {
+            return wanted;
+        };
+        // Finer: past the finer level's edge by a sixth; coarser: below the
+        // current level's edge by a sixth.
+        let edge = if to < at {
+            self.sim[to].0 * 7.0 / 6.0
+        } else {
+            self.sim[at].0 * 5.0 / 6.0
+        };
+        let past = if to < at {
+            pixels >= edge
+        } else {
+            pixels < edge
+        };
+        if past { wanted } else { current }
+    }
+
+    /// One band throughout: the given form at every distance, with this
+    /// policy's shading.
+    pub fn fixed(&self, form: Form) -> Self {
+        Self {
+            bands: vec![Band {
+                min_pixels: 0.0,
+                form,
+            }],
+            ..self.clone()
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// What to draw for a head `pixels` tall. Within a band of strands the
+    /// share rises smoothly towards the next finer band's, so moving in
+    /// grows the count rather than stepping it.
+    pub fn select(&self, pixels: f32, lods: LodCounts) -> Representation {
+        self.select_blended(pixels, lods).0
+    }
+
+    /// What to draw for a head `pixels` tall, and the coarser form fading
+    /// in under it near the bottom of its band. At the band's lower edge
+    /// the blend is all the coarser form, which is what the band below
+    /// draws at its top: the hand-over is continuous.
+    pub fn select_blended(&self, pixels: f32, lods: LodCounts) -> (Representation, Option<Blend>) {
+        let at = self.band(pixels);
+        let form = self.form(at, pixels, lods);
+        let lo = self.bands[at].min_pixels;
+        if self.blend <= 0.0 || at + 1 >= self.bands.len() || lo <= 0.0 {
+            return (form, None);
+        }
+        let amount = 1.0 - (pixels - lo) / (lo * self.blend);
+        if amount <= 0.0 {
+            return (form, None);
+        }
+        let to = self.form(at + 1, lo, lods);
+        (
+            form,
+            Some(Blend {
+                to,
+                amount: amount.min(1.0),
+            }),
+        )
+    }
+
+    fn band(&self, pixels: f32) -> usize {
+        self.bands
+            .iter()
+            .position(|b| pixels >= b.min_pixels)
+            .unwrap_or(self.bands.len() - 1)
+    }
+
+    /// Band `at`'s form for a head `pixels` tall.
+    fn form(&self, at: usize, pixels: f32, lods: LodCounts) -> Representation {
+        let total = lods.strands;
+        match self.bands[at].form {
+            Form::Cards { level } => Representation::Cards {
+                level: level.min(lods.cards.saturating_sub(1)),
+            },
+            Form::Strands { level, share } => {
+                let mut share = share;
+                if at > 0
+                    && let Form::Strands { share: finer, .. } = self.bands[at - 1].form
+                {
+                    let lo = self.bands[at].min_pixels;
+                    let hi = self.bands[at - 1].min_pixels;
+                    let t = ((pixels - lo) / (hi - lo).max(1.0)).clamp(0.0, 1.0);
+                    share += (finer - share) * t;
+                }
+                let count = ((total as f32 * share).round() as usize).clamp(1.min(total), total);
+                Representation::Strands {
+                    level: level.min(lods.levels.saturating_sub(1)),
+                    count,
+                    width_scale: total as f32 / count.max(1) as f32,
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// The strands that cast shadows: the policy's shadow level and share.
+    pub fn shadow(&self, lods: LodCounts) -> Representation {
+        let total = lods.strands;
+        let count =
+            ((total as f32 * self.shadow_share).round() as usize).clamp(1.min(total), total);
+        Representation::Strands {
+            level: self.shadow_level.min(lods.levels.saturating_sub(1)),
+            count,
+            width_scale: total as f32 / count.max(1) as f32,
+        }
+    }
+}
